{"title":"2022 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Dot_Product)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Dot Product)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Complex_Numbers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Complex Numbers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(1-16)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(1-16)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ef70e0b09d406a3feab5606b22893424a777a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+2x-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> intersects the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0d168b2f59134516b99bbd615508264569ccf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\angle ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91be4b2a777e10f0b23ba16d231f6135c66b8e1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{7} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"404\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e194e324298623df885f21dfe4a7f70b72af7c0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(250);   real xMin = -15; real xMax = 15; real yMin = -17; real yMax = 17;  draw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2));  real f(real x) { return x^2+2*x-15; } draw(graph(f,-6.75,4.75),red);  pair A, B, C; A = (-5,0); B = (0,-15); C = (3,0);  draw(A--B--C); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5NW,linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5SE,linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5NE,linewidth(4.5));  label(&quot;$y=x^2+2x-15$&quot;,(12,9),red); [/asy]\" width=\"385\" height=\"418\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Dot_Product.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Dot_Product)\">Solution 1 (Dot Product)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Dot Product)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc2cd0325da171b6c2292c8b530aeffa0be1783.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(-5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7ba2165904ee9161186d65946af11613e7208b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(0,-15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae12b55ecc44d00856033eb7bc418c3a265a88eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. Create vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32c97d25a691260cd76758521bbece87f5aaef7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/41921b1c7131c0f8fbac792acaa1f7a20b18555c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{BC}.$\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" /> These can be reduced to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/a/f7a00c922f5b9086d07f4b805f000e9e8251b14f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle -1, 3 \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f8868aa4e6ea23c815123cf59e78ff1494fbc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\langle 1, 5 \\rangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, respectively. Then, we can use the dot product to calculate the cosine of the angle (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07bf5cccb2a5ca11b46125d7e47d30dd5e483ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\angle ABC$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />) between them:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d4eba1b2dd993341a8320fd799c67595768d62.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\langle -1, 3 \\rangle \\cdot \\langle 1, 5 \\rangle = 15-1 &amp;= \\sqrt{10}\\sqrt{26}\\cos(\\theta),\\\\ \\implies \\cos (\\theta) &amp;= \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{65}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"325\" height=\"70\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31406d851941b3822d34c9a4d34c95293f45dc4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\angle ABC) = \\sqrt{\\frac{65}{49}-1}= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~Jackson La Vallee\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/e/59ef70e0b09d406a3feab5606b22893424a777a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2+2x-15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> intersects the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c6d8abfb452e39157f93c7dc806649a81e9bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6a917716191facf6d17308cdb8119392b77732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. Without loss of generality, let these points be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Also, the graph intersects the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c247836aa62503a4d9aad532f53eb9040660f662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (0, -15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708828d1767ada30291be13089b0c9711b8e14a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O=(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e44c01c0ed926b86414a0fbedc2fe1d2eaa9b871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/7/41752e67cd033c961edd7532c9376bc82296d255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BOC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> are right triangles. \n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/1/1f13b31a2d031cae9b5657b213b53df5cae8d2c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\angle ABC) = \\tan(\\angle ABO + \\angle OBC) = \\frac{\\tan(\\angle ABO) + \\tan(\\angle OBC)}{1 - \\tan(\\angle ABO) \\cdot \\tan(\\angle OBC)} = \\frac{\\frac15 + \\frac13}{1 - \\frac1{15}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.\\]\" width=\"713\" height=\"49\" /> \nAlternatively, we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7624b7a61c4c83e3d9eef4acd40954ee7ce2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 5 \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31d172ac26165231c926cea78169629865a89a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 3 \\sqrt{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> and then use the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/405bafb1a1021e768c3ab8c60594143193cc2f71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac12 ab \\sin \\angle C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area_of_a_Triangle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area of a Triangle\">area formula for a triangle</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d0d168b2f59134516b99bbd615508264569ccf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\angle ABC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like above, we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/8406e5f7c765b5c5fcd22a3c9a756da79907ca29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/4/99440c769639befc66dc651a71b63738b6041c12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, -15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, then finding via the Pythagorean Theorem that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/7/cc7624b7a61c4c83e3d9eef4acd40954ee7ce2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 5 \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31d172ac26165231c926cea78169629865a89a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 3 \\sqrt{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />. Using the Law of Cosines, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/9/589092c2fc1ec3adb5d87789c6149add273f392c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(\\angle ABC) = \\frac{AB^2 + BC^2 - AC^2}{2 AB BC} = \\frac{250 + 234 - 64}{30 \\sqrt{260}} = \\frac{7}{\\sqrt{65}}.\\]\" width=\"484\" height=\"44\" /> Then, we use the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/e/e4e22202074d07c0dc2d3ebcfbafe4534fa579c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2(x) = \\sec^2(x) - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"21\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/7/2f70aafc7d45e13af999df6d168db78d0c37b1e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan(\\angle ABC) = \\sqrt{\\frac{65}{49} - 1} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~ jamesl123456\n</p><p>Alternatively, we could observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fe09113b61bae229f7f0a615b40cb6015c5748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle ABC)=\\sqrt{1-\\cos^2(\\angle ABC)}=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\dfrac7{\\sqrt{65}}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\dfrac{16}{65}}=\\dfrac4{\\sqrt{65}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"538\" height=\"56\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31eb899bdbb3c3857d24ef0d29c1ae1a3c76026d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\angle ABC)=\\dfrac{\\sin(\\angle ABC)}{\\cos(\\angle ABC)}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac47}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"302\" height=\"49\" />. \n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can reflect the figure, but still have the same angle. This problem is the same as having points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93ad1f26dec0ab2d236723d58715c2fe86a831cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f957579485ef4c8bfc1a3748a1400e3158251e39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(3,15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd16116efc0e74269e94def870a9dbd41d7b4b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(-5,15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />, where we're solving for angle FED. We can use the formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e238eaaf8c240c1709629c4135d4f11b84063c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> to solve now where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis to angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis to angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995ece4287f7c447c4ec517ad0d2f3e451be66e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(a) = \\textrm{slope of line }DF = -3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/200411a8d91ce831451366daf9652f226d4fa2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(B) = \\textrm{slope of line }DE = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />. Plugging these values into the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e238eaaf8c240c1709629c4135d4f11b84063c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(a-b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" /> formula, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4fd077e9dc1abc6a45dfa595a559b8860d2ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3-5)/(1+(-3\\cdot 5))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/e/a3e30e40a0f62b7875c2e7b38ef0ff8eb533edf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"64\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~mathboy100 (minor LaTeX edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/9/6d9b6009e3e1ca77c8683e8c37776da703e4a1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin{C}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> has side-lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a10b621cb974ff395ceef7e1947fe0b9eecef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=5\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819e44836d4493d581398447652f24cb6f2d64ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=3\\sqrt{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" /> from Pythagorean theorem, with the area being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24bfa84f07afb67b37cdb8d13e03e45a2689b00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12\\cdot8\\cdot15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We equate the areas together to get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/569d5e7d37ed91b6c7a511798fd1195cab0a1d20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12\\cdot8\\cdot15=\\frac12\\cdot5\\sqrt{10}\\cdot3\\sqrt{26}\\cdot\\sin{B},\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"37\" />\nfrom which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac2ca87a97a0a290598a15f7822940a1592e68b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{B}=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{260}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"118\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>From Pythagorean Identity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/30994da4bf3f19c816f983fcff016e848dc6f65b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{B}=\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{260}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Then we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f14359a3b9966bf5ff81bb66d4cb3a40d2186700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{B}=\\frac{\\sin{B}}{\\cos{B}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"39\" />, to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/5/d95858af70699afb3dde9221480438fb78462af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{B}=\\frac{8}{14}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"179\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>- SAHANWIJETUNGA\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Complex_Numbers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Complex_Numbers)\">Solution 6 (Complex Numbers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Complex Numbers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/f/f1f4c72e41448b6f9dd579ee6a92fd6d8c57294d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(300);   real xMin = -15; real xMax = 15; real yMin = -17; real yMax = 17;  draw((xMin,0)--(xMax,0),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,yMin)--(0,yMax),black+linewidth(1.5),EndArrow(5)); label(&quot;$x$&quot;,(xMax,0),(2,0)); label(&quot;$y$&quot;,(0,yMax),(0,2));  real f(real x) { return x^2+2*x-15; } draw(graph(f,-6.75,4.75),red);  pair A, B, C, O; A = (-5,0); B = (0,-15); C = (3,0); O = origin;  markscalefactor=0.1; draw(rightanglemark(B,O,C)); draw(A--B--C); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,1.5SW,linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,1.5SE,linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5SE,linewidth(4.5)); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,1.5SW,linewidth(4.5));  label(&quot;$y=x^2+2x-15$&quot;,(12,9),red); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,(-2.5,0),1.5N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(1.5,0),1.5N); label(&quot;$15$&quot;,(0,-6),W);  label(&quot;$\\theta$&quot;,(0,-15),9*dir(100)); label(&quot;$\\phi$&quot;,(0,-15),9*dir(84)); [/asy]\" width=\"452\" height=\"502\" />\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a344f239a0541c7fb07f41290ec03cadd529c227.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + 2x - 15 = (x-3)(x+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"21\" />, we may assume, without loss of generality, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-intercepts of the given parabola are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99fc156e6ecd3068051666852cb9dbec76a1da3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(-5,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/f/fdf0974f9f44880775816da149590408ce67c50e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />. And, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> has coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55190e9a8d68d94de7675270545249d61f742fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,-15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Consider complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f002afaad3b0c96874adaa01c17ac60bf44f522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 3 + i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bff79416f0d37b7c6eb1633028b4b3d43464e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w = 5 + i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" /> whose arguments are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1fbbe4316d751edc9cab8b1546bc6cb4ac6bacf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta \\coloneqq \\angle OBA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f4934d19411ff70116d770bfbc95a12eb1398531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi \\coloneqq \\angle OBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />, respectively. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe94826285ec924b4d844a94a730cb9a66c7a002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\theta + \\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" /> is the argument of the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c238a0e2fe6d3fd49d5219a4b5fabdbf6b5fb4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$zw$\" width=\"22\" height=\"8\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0ac768c999876dfd1f4c586a8e1b4bd678d30fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[zw = (3+i)(5+i) = 14 + 8i.\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"18\" />\nHence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44080d425a69bd6bb9bf0070a3f6502953b13fa7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan \\angle ABC = \\frac{\\operatorname{Im}(zw)}{\\operatorname{Re}(zw)} = \\frac{8}{14} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{4}{7}}.\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~VensL.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by mop 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ezGvZgBLe8k&amp;t=458s\">https://youtu.be/ezGvZgBLe8k&amp;t=458s</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/InJgY_JYBkE\">https://youtu.be/InJgY_JYBkE</a>\n</p><p>~<i>Education, the Study of Everything</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.281-16.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(1-16)\">Video Solution(1-16)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(1-16)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g\">https://youtu.be/SCwQ9jUfr0g</a>\n</p><p>~~Hayabusa1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B\">2022 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2022 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></